### Photos

No photo set has been confirmed. Source order:

1. **A local folder of the client's real work.** If the folder contains `before`, `after`, `lawn`, `garden`, or phone-camera images, run the full pipeline below on them. Never substitute stock while usable real photos exist.
2. **The business's own Google Business Profile photos (the "By owner" tab).** If the browser tools are available, pull what's usable. Their own photos of their own work are fair game for their own site. Log where each came from.
3. **Licensed stock, last resort, hero texture only.** Real-looking Gold Coast or subtropical lawn and garden scenes. No visible brands, no people's faces, no stock photo that obviously reads as another country (no autumn leaves, no snow, no English cottage borders). Never use stock for the work gallery.

**Pipeline (for any real photo set):**
- Inventory every file and note what each one actually shows (lawn, hedge, garden bed, cleanup, before, after).
- Rename to `lowercase-kebab-case-descriptive.jpg`, for example `freshly-mown-front-lawn-edged-driveway.jpg`. Never leave `IMG_1234.jpg`.
- Sort into a **featured set** (best 4 to 6, for the home page) and a **full set** (for the work page).
- Write specific alt text per image describing what is visible.
- Generate `.webp` copies alongside the originals, serve with `<picture>`.
- Keep any before/after pairs together and labelled as a pair.
- Write a small `images/manifest.json` recording the original filename, new filename, alt text, set (featured or full), and source (client folder, Google profile, or stock).

If fewer than 6 genuinely usable real photos exist, do NOT pad the work page with stock. Say so in your handoff message and build the work page with only what's real.

