## 10. Technical, SEO and Accessibility Checklist

- Semantic HTML5 throughout, one `h1` per page, logical heading order.
- `<picture>` with `.webp` and a fallback `<img>` that has `width` and `height` attributes. `loading="lazy"` on everything below the fold. Hero image NOT lazy.
- Unique, descriptive alt text on every image. Decorative images get `alt=""`.
- Per-page `<title>` and `<meta name="description">`. Suggested:
  - Home: `Maik Gardens | Lawn Mowing and Gardening, Gold Coast`
  - Services: `Services | Maik Gardens, Gold Coast Lawn and Garden Care`
  - Work: `Our Work | Maik Gardens`
  - Contact: `Contact | Maik Gardens, Call 0406 851 039`
  Meta descriptions: plain sentences, under 160 characters, no em dashes.
- Open Graph tags (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image`, `og:type`) using the real hero image, and a favicon made from the badge.
- **JSON-LD** `LocalBusiness` (or `HomeAndConstructionBusiness`) on the home page: `name`, `telephone` ("+61406851039"), `areaServed` "Gold Coast", `address` with `addressLocality` "Broadbeach Waters", `addressRegion` "QLD", `addressCountry` "AU". **No `streetAddress`. No `aggregateRating`** (self-published review markup breaks Google's guidelines and the count is not independently verifiable from the site).
- Visible focus outlines never suppressed. `aria-label` on every icon-only control.
- WCAG AA contrast checked on the real palette pairings used.
- No console errors, no broken links, no unused CSS at handoff.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` everywhere.

